  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/hemichromis-sp-red-gabon/",
      "html": "<p>Red Jewel Cichlids are gorgeous fishes with splendid coloration and fascinating behaviour. They form a biparental family: both male and female take care of the offspring together. The only negative aspect is that they can be really nasty against tankmates, especially when they have young (and they almost always have young). The degree of aggressiveness depends both on the individual and on the respective strain.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/hemichromis-sp-red-gabon/",
      "html": "<p>Hemichromis sp. Red Gabon belongs, technically speaking, to the species Hemichromis stellifer. However, there are many differences in coloration between this Gabon population (the specimens described are German-bred ones) and the population from the Congo, from where H. stellifer was scientifically described. So prudent people prefer to name the fish \"sp. Gabon\". This Red Jewel is extremely colorful and belongs to the more peaceful members of its kind. In densely populated tanks, hardly ever even a small fin damage can be spotted.</p>"
    }
  ],
